the cycle-accurate rz1600 reference emulator.
<http://www.github.com/quxrzd/er1600>

+================+


## ABOUT:
+=======+
er1600 is a cycle-accurate rz1600 C++ emulator library that
attempts to act as a reference emulator.


## BUILD:
+=======+
er1600 requires a C++11 compiler and make.
"all", "run", and "clr" targets can be used.

on a unix-like machine, run the following:
$ make -f mkf <target>

replace <target> with the target of choice. 


## HACKING:
+=========+
hacking around is simple: clone er1600:
$ git clone http://github.com/quxrzd/er1600

after that, copy the src/er1600 directory and implement it
into your own project(s) by including the er1600.h++ file.

microcode.c++ implements microcode functions from
er1600.h++. er1600.c++ uses the microcode functions from
microcode.c++. prg.c++ is an implementation of the er1600
library. 


